---
giftFundsBody: We're raising $5,000 by September 26 to fund legal research that
  will strengthen our position. Every dollar goes toward that specific purpose.
  The BAA will engage the law firm of Thompson & Hine to prepare an in-depth
  legal analysis of the legal and risk issues involved in a transfer of the
  endowment. The results of that analysis will guide our negotiation with the
  university. We are in active dialogue with Denison leadership about the
  endowment's future, and this legal analysis is key to achieving an acceptable
  resolution that preserves the promise.
layout: base.njk
tags: navItem
navLabel: "Give Now"
navOrder: 2
showInNav: false
title: Support the Endowment Campaign — Denison BAA
description: Help fund the legal research strengthening the BAA's position as we
  work with Denison University to protect the BAA Scholarship Endowment's
  promise to Black students.
askHeadline: Help Us Protect The Promise
askBody: We're raising $5,000 by September 26 to fund legal research in support
  of the BAA's position as we sit down with Denison University leadership about
  the BAA Scholarship Endowment.
storyBody: For over two decades, Black alumni gave to the BAA Scholarship
  Endowment believing it would always serve Black students at Denison, the way
  it was intended to from the start. That commitment hasn't changed. What has
  changed is the environment, and it's on us to make sure the fund still does
  what our community built it to do. Denison has asked the BAA to consent to an
  amendment of the gift agreement which governs the BAA Scholarship Endowment,
  that would change it from an identity-based award to a need-based award. It
  would become a generic scholarship award no longer set aside for Black
  students, contrary to the BAA's intent. The BAA has refused consent to such an
  amendment and will not now nor in the future consent to any change that will
  diminish the Black-serving purpose of the BAA endowment.
freefunderLink: "[FREEFUNDER LINK]"
whereThingsStandBody: This work is part of an active, ongoing dialogue between
  the BAA and Denison about the future of the endowment. Based on our review of
  the legal information available, the BAA's preferred resolution is transfer of
  the endowment to a new steward that is not prohibited from administering the
  endowment according to its donor intent. A review of preliminary legal
  research leads us to conclude that there is a viable legal pathway for
  transfer of the endowment to a new steward. To date, Denison's response has
  been that they do not believe such a transfer is lawful. Denison has not
  provided the BAA with any legal analysis or legal opinion to support this
  assertion.
howHandledBody: Unlike previous fundraising appeals where the BAA raised funds
  under Denison's tax-exempt status, this campaign will be conducted under the
  BAA's own EIN. The BAA is an unincorporated association without tax-exempt
  status, so your gift for this purpose is not tax-deductible. Every dollar
  raised in this campaign will support the legal research that backs the BAA's
  position. This isn't a general fund. It's a specific, time-bound need with a
  specific purpose — giving our position the weight it deserves when we sit down
  at the negotiating table.
whosBehindBody: "This effort is led by the BAA Executive Board: Aaron Laramore
  (President), Martin Jones (Vice President), Demitrus Evans (Secretary), Makiva
  McIntosh (Treasurer), Felice Harris (Historian), and James Thornton
  (Parliamentarian), and supported by the BAA membership. Together, we are an
  alumni community working in unison to protect the promise we made to future
  generations of Denisonians.  "
---

